# Regression model for the reverse bimolecular state-change corrections in
# issue #8.  No input under sample_inputs/ contains a bimolecular state change,
# so that code path is not covered by the validation suite.
#
# The reaction order matters.  The first reaction is irreversible, so it takes
# forwardRxns[0] without creating a BackRxn.  The bimolecular state change is
# therefore forwardRxns[1] with conjBackRxnIndex == 0 -- precisely the
# arrangement the master code could not handle:
#
#   * its gate required conjBackRxnIndex > 0, and 0 fails that test, so the
#     reverse (Y -> X) state change was never even considered;
#   * had the gate passed, it recovered the rate index by subtracting pointers
#     into two unrelated vectors, never assigned rateIndex on a single match,
#     and read element 0 of an empty match list when nothing matched;
#   * downstream, perform_bimolecular_state_change_* indexed backRxns with the
#     forward index, which is backRxns[1] here and out of range.
#
# Expected outcome: under the master build A(a~Y) only grows, because just the
# forward X -> Y direction can fire.  Under the corrected build the two states
# reach a steady state set by onRate3Dka and offRatekb.
#
# The K(kd) + K(kd) association at the end is scaffolding, not part of the test.
# set_rMaxLimit() in master only inspects ReactionType::bimolecular, so a model
# whose only bimolecular reaction is a state change leaves rMaxLimit at 0, and
# SimulVolume::Dimensions then divides the box length by that zero, producing a
# negative cell count and an endless "CELL PAIR MAX EXCEEDED" rescale.  This
# reaction gives rMaxLimit a sane value.  Its rates are low enough that it stays
# a minor perturbation, and it is listed last so the state-change reaction keeps
# indices 1 and 0.

start parameters
    nItr = 200000
    timeStep = 0.1

    timeWrite = 500
    trajWrite = 1000000
    restartWrite = 1000000
    pdbWrite = 1000000
end parameters

start boundaries
    WaterBox = [100.0,100.0,100.0] #nm
end boundaries

start molecules
    K : 30
    A : 200 (a~X)
end molecules

start reactions
    # forwardRxns[0], irreversible, so no BackRxn is created and the forward and
    # back index spaces diverge from here on.  Rate 0 keeps it from firing, so it
    # only shifts the indices.
    A(a~X) -> A(a~Y)
    rate = 0.0

    # forwardRxns[1] / backRxns[0]: enzyme-facilitated state change.
    K(k) + A(a~X) <-> K(k) + A(a~Y)
    onRate3Dka = 10.0
    offRatekb = 50.0
    sigma = 1.0
    norm1 = [0,0,1]
    norm2 = [0,0,1]
    assocAngles = [nan,nan,nan,nan,nan]

    # forwardRxns[2] / backRxns[1]: scaffolding, see the note above.
    K(kd) + K(kd) <-> K(kd!1).K(kd!1)
    onRate3Dka = 0.01
    offRatekb = 100.0
    sigma = 1.0
    norm1 = [0,0,1]
    norm2 = [0,0,1]
    assocAngles = [nan,nan,nan,nan,nan]
end reactions
